# Auto-Pigeon EricW tools @VERSION@ — @PLATFORM@

This is an **unsigned development build** of the **Auto-Pigeon fork** of ericw-tools, the Quake
map compilers by Eric Wasylishen and contributors. It is not an upstream release.

| | |
| --- | --- |
| Release | `@TAG@` |
| Fork commit | `@COMMIT@` — <@FORK@/commit/@COMMIT@> |
| Upstream base | `@UPSTREAM_DESCRIBE@` of <@UPSTREAM@> |
| Version banner | `@STAMP@` |
| Target | @PLATFORM@ |

The fork adds one compiler change to upstream `main`: `SplitBrush` splits thin brush fragments
with `PLANESIDE_EPSILON` instead of `0.1`, which closes a clip-hull leak through valid thin
geometry, together with its regression test. Upstream has not reviewed or accepted that change.

## Layout

```text
@STEM@/
  bin/            qbsp vis light bspinfo bsputil maputil, and the libraries they load
  licenses/       GPL texts and the notices of every library in bin/
  README.md       this file
  build-info.json what was built, from what, with what
  MANIFEST.json   every file of this archive with its size, mode and SHA-256
```

`bin/` is self-contained: keep the programs and the libraries beside them together. The folder
may live anywhere, including a path with spaces. Nothing needs to be installed, and nothing
here downloads or updates anything.

## Requirements

@REQUIREMENTS@

## Use

@USAGE@

Every program prints `ericw-tools @STAMP@` in its first lines; that string is how to tell this
build from an upstream one.

## Verify

Compare the ZIP with the `SHA256SUMS` file of the same release before unpacking. A SHA-256 proves
the download is intact; it is not a signature and says nothing about who built it.

